    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the lighter pressure helps, but I'm still seeing some tearing on the end grain. i've tried changing the direction of my paring, but it's like the wood just wants to split right at the point. could it be the moisture content of the walnut? or maybe i need a different kind of bevel on my chisel specifically for these fine pins?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
