      "content": "Moisture content can indeed affect how the wood splits. If the walnut is too dry, it might be more prone to splitting. Try acclimating the wood to your shop environment or using a conditioner. Regarding your chisel, you might want to use a shallow bevel or a diamond-set corner chisel, as these shapes are designed to cut fine internal angles and prevent tearing in the end grain.",
