      "content": "Wood characteristics can certainly be inconsistent, but ensuring steady support and consistent technique is key. Try to clamp down your piece as securely as possible to prevent movement or vibration. It's also possible that the internal structure of the wood, such as the direction of the growth rings or knots, could be affecting your cuts—this is harder to detect but could inform your approach. Take breaks to better observe the grain and the wood's behavior, and adjust your technique accordingly. If necessary, mark incrementally and make small adjustments rather than trying to take everything in at once.",
